    "intro_html":  "Panang is the thick one. Where green curry runs loose and soupy, panang reduces down until it coats the back of a spoon, and it gets its roundness from ground peanuts worked right into the paste. We build the paste from scratch here with dried chiles, peanuts, lemongrass, ginger and garlic, which sounds ambitious until you realize it is one blender and four minutes. Each bowl comes in at \u003cstrong\u003e592 calories and 26 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.90\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
